[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4399002271","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119312#issuecomment-4399002271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119312","id":4399002271,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBjNynw","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-07T16:29:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T16:29:33Z","body":"> Positioning of accessibility region is still borked for submenus.\r\n> Scaling a parent Node2D still results in borked sizing/positioning of the accessibility region.\r\n\r\nMost likely is the issue with all nested popups, not specifically menus, I'll check it.\r\n\r\n> ui_focus_next/ui_focus_prev does nothing when search bar is focused.\r\n\r\nI guess these should do the same UP/DOWN actions do and release the focus.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4399002271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4406605567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119312#issuecomment-4406605567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119312","id":4406605567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBqd2_w","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T13:02:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T13:02:17Z","body":"> Most likely is the issue with all nested popups, not specifically menus, I'll check it.\r\n\r\nMade a draft for position fix https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119328, will check scaling issues on weekend (probably scale need to be applied to the same transform).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4406605567/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4406676051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119312#issuecomment-4406676051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119312","id":4406676051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBqiKUw","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T13:12:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T13:14:02Z","body":"> I guess these should do the same UP/DOWN actions do and release the focus.\r\n\r\nI managed to solve this without dealing with the events explicitly, by instead just enabling `FOCUS_ALL` on `PopupMenu::control` and having its `focus_entered` select the first item if none were selected. This also meant I could have `ui_up`/`ui_down` do `control->grab_focus()` rather than `search_bar->release_focus()`.\r\n\r\nThis did however (perhaps unsurprisingly) result in the `control` itself becoming the focus for the screen reader, but it seems that just introducing the same `PopupMenuItems` class found in #118886 and forwarding its `get_focused_accessibility_element` to `PopupMenu` fixed that problem. It feels a bit hacky though, I'll admit.\r\n\r\nI also had to throw in some hacky handling of `ui_up` (and `ui_down`) in the `gui_input` of this new `PopupMenuItems` class to stop it from switching focus to `search_bar`, because of how the input handling is dealt with in `PopupMenu` in general.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I still felt like this was all preferrable to handling `ui_focus_next`/`ui_focus_prev` explicitly, since we're now just relying on the existing focus machinery, but I'll happily change it if you disagree.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4406676051/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4432590066","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119312#issuecomment-4432590066","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119312","id":4432590066,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCDP08g","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-12T16:22:02Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T14:58:30Z","body":"Needs rebase","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https